from contracts import obj, arr, S, I, enum

SCOPE = obj(decisions=arr(obj(regulation=S, decision=enum('include', 'exclude', 'uncertain'), reason=S, quote=S)))
SCOPE_TASK = '''Assess the applicability of EVERY supplied regulation to the supplied product, using only supplied source editions and product facts. Include obligations for the component, installation and its stated functions. Distinguish required performance from unrelated systems. Do not infer that passive materials require approval as a different device. If a supplied source explicitly consolidates earlier regulations, avoid imposing both alternative approval routes; explain the source basis. If applicability depends on missing facts, say uncertain. Each decision must quote exact text from that regulation's supplied profile. No gold answers or regulation IDs from memory. Return exactly one decision per regulation. Quotes are evidence for your reasoning, not proof that all obligations apply.'''

REQ = obj(text=S, quote=S)
EXTRACT = obj(decisions=arr(obj(id=S, decision=enum('relevant', 'irrelevant', 'unresolved'), reason=S,
                              requirements=arr(REQ))))
EXTRACT_TASK = '''Assess EVERY target clause against the product. Context records are supporting evidence only, not targets. Return exactly one decision per target ID. Extract all independent applicable engineering obligations, preserving conditions, exceptions, numerical limits, tests, marking and production conformity. Never invent unspecified product functions. A conditional obligation may apply without claiming the condition always holds. Pure headings, definitions and approval authority procedures usually produce no engineering requirement, but definitions constrain interpretation. Relevant context may have zero requirements. Each proposed requirement must have a verbatim quote from its own target text; use context to preserve governing conditions. Tables/figures that cannot be interpreted from text, missing references or missing product facts stay unresolved. Requirements must be at most 1800 characters each. Do not output requirements for irrelevant/unresolved targets. Do not replace detailed obligations with a broad umbrella summary. Use no reference answer.'''

VERIFY = obj(decisions=arr(obj(id=S, decision=enum('keep', 'drop', 'unresolved'), reason=S)))
VERIFY_TASK = '''Independently verify EVERY proposed requirement against the supplied product, its complete source clause and supporting context. Return exactly one decision per ID. Keep only obligations that are source-supported and applicable, with conditions, exceptions, scope and numerical details preserved. Drop inapplicable or unsupported proposals. Mark unresolved when the provided evidence is insufficient. Do not discard a valid obligation merely because it is conditional. Do not use ranking scores as evidence. Do not invent facts or rewrite the requirements.'''
